      "content": "thanks for those. i noticed you're focusing a lot on CRT and intersectionality to explain these gaps. i've heard some people argue that focusing too much on those theories can ignore other important factors like individual financial choices or broader economic shifts that aren't necessarily about race. how would you incorporate or address those different perspectives in the curriculum so the students get a full picture?",
